    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "A queue is a type of data structure in programming which allows elements to be added at the back and removed from the front. It is similar to a queue in real-life."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Think of it as a ticket queue outside a cinema hall, where the first person entering the queue is the first person who gets the ticket."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "That is why the queue is also known as a First in First Out data structure."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The elements of the queue data structure are:"
    },
    {
      "type": "bullet_list",
      "items": [
        "rear - the back part of the queue to which data is added",
        "front - the front part of the queue from which data is removed"
      ]
    },
